N1  - Price and colleagues compare turnover categories with differing referee discretion to investigate NBA officiating patterns. Their abstract reports advantages for home teams and teams trailing in games or playoff series. I will use the identification idea to motivate controls, while treating this source as preliminary until its full methods and results are available.
N1  - Methods: Compares discretionary and less discretionary turnovers as a player-behavior control. Exact published sample [uncertain].
N1  - Findings: Abstract reports evidence favoring home teams, teams trailing within games, and teams trailing in playoff series.
N1  - Limits: Full robustness and identification assumptions [uncertain]; turnover categories do not directly identify defensive-foul bias.
N1  - Evidence: Publisher abstract only.
